<section id="about">
  <h2>What I Do</h2>
  <p>
    I'm a Senior AI Engineer at Consensys, where I build AI systems people use
    every day: retrieval-based search, agents, data pipelines, support
    automation end to end. I also built and ran the AI team inside our customer
    success department, which meant designing how a whole department would work
    with these tools, not just writing the code.
  </p>
  <p>
    Out of that I built a framework for using AI well. I made it because I
    needed one, and it's what I work from now when I help businesses adopt AI in
    a way that fits the people doing the work. Most adoption starts with the
    tool and expects the humans to adjust around it. I'd rather start with the
    humans and choose the tools to fit.
  </p>

  <h2>Why</h2>
  <p>
    Technology should be at the service of a more human life. I believe that
    plainly, and I've spent enough time inside these systems to know it doesn't
    happen on its own.
  </p>
  <p>
    In practice it comes down to three questions: which parts of your work you
    should actually hand over, how you keep the parts that are yours, and what
    you do with the time once you get it back. Answered well, AI gives you room.
    Answered badly, it gives you more of the same work, faster.
  </p>

  <h2>What I Love</h2>
  <p>
    Outside work I dance, I hike, I build things with my hands, and I spend as
    much time outdoors as I can get away with. None of it is productive, which
    is the point. It's also the honest answer to why I care about any of this:
    the time these tools give back has to go somewhere, and this is where mine
    goes.
  </p>

  <div class="signature">
    <p>— Sara</p>
  </div>
</section>

